  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat the oven to 300°F.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Cut buns into 1-inch cubes, then divide between two large baking sheet pans. Place baking sheets in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and bake, stirring every 10 minutes, until bread is dried out, about 25 minutes. Remove from oven and set aside to cool, about 20 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the bread is cooling, fold a 30-inch long piece of aluminum foil in thirds lengthwise to create a \"collar\" for your slow cooker insert. Place the collar in the slow cooker, pressing it against the sides of the insert, then coat with cooking spray. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 spritz nonstick cooking spray"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place milk, cream, chocolate hazelnut spread, eggs, sugar, and salt in a large bowl. Whisk until sugar is dissolved and custard is combined, about 1 minute.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 cups whole milk\n1 ½ cups heavy whipping cream\n1 cup chocolate hazelnut spread\n¾ cup granulated sugar\n¼ tsp salt"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add dried bread cubes and chocolate chips to the bowl with the custard, then stir to combine. Set aside for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the custard is mostly absorbed.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup dark chocolate chips"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer soaked bread to the slow cooker, spread out in an even layer, and sprinkle with additional chocolate chips. Cover and cook until the bread pudding is set, LOW for 3-4 hours.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup dark chocolate chips"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the bread pudding is done, remove from heat and set aside to cool slightly, about 30 minutes. Remove foil collar.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide bread pudding between plates or bowls and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
